---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import site from '../data/site.json';

const { url } = site;

const schema = `{
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@graph": [
    {
      "@type": "PrivacyPolicyPage",
      "@id": "${url}/privacy#webpage",
      "url": "${url}/privacy",
      "name": "Privacy Policy | STLACCESS",
      "description": "A plain-English breakdown of how I handle your data. 100% cookie-free, no tracking, and zero personal data collection.",
      "isPartOf": { "@id": "${url}/#website" }
    },
    {
      "@type": "BreadcrumbList",
      "itemListElement": [
        { "@type": "ListItem", "position": 1, "name": "Home", "item": "${url}/" },
        { "@type": "ListItem", "position": 2, "name": "Privacy" }
      ]
    }
  ]
}`;
---
<Layout
  title="Privacy Policy | STLACCESS"
  description="Simple, transparent privacy policy for STLACCESS users. No accounts, no tracking, just precision."
  schema={schema}
>
  <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-6 py-20 w-full">
    <!-- Breadcrumbs -->
    <nav class="max-w-6xl mx-auto pt-12 pb-4 text-[10px] font-black uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-slate-600" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
      <a href="/" class="hover:text-[#ff6b35]">Home</a>
      <span class="mx-2 text-slate-800">/</span>
      <span class="text-slate-400">Privacy Policy</span>
    </nav>

    <!-- Header -->
    <div class="mb-16">
      <h1 class="text-4xl md:text-6xl font-bold font-heading mb-6 tracking-tight">Privacy <span class="text-[#ff6b35]">Policy</span></h1>
      <p class="text-lg text-slate-400 leading-relaxed max-w-2xl">I believe your scale data should stay exactly where it belongs: with you. Here is exactly how I handle your information.</p>
    </div>

    <section class="space-y-16">
      <!-- Key Points Grid -->
      <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-3 gap-6">
        <div class="bg-slate-900/30 p-8 rounded-3xl border border-white/5">
          <div class="w-10 h-10 bg-[#ff6b35]/10 rounded-xl flex items-center justify-center mb-6">
            <i class="fa-solid fa-user-slash text-[#ff6b35]"></i>
          </div>
          <h3 class="font-bold text-white mb-2">No Accounts</h3>
          <p class="text-sm text-slate-400">I don't ask for your name, email, or any personal details to use the tools.</p>
        </div>
        
        <div class="bg-slate-900/30 p-8 rounded-3xl border border-white/5">
          <div class="w-10 h-10 bg-[#ff6b35]/10 rounded-xl flex items-center justify-center mb-6">
            <i class="fa-solid fa-hard-drive text-[#ff6b35]"></i>
          </div>
          <h3 class="font-bold text-white mb-2">Local Storage</h3>
          <p class="text-sm text-slate-400">Your custom library info stays saved strictly inside your own browser's memory.</p>
        </div>
        
        <div class="bg-slate-900/30 p-8 rounded-3xl border border-white/5">
          <div class="w-10 h-10 bg-[#ff6b35]/10 rounded-xl flex items-center justify-center mb-6">
            <i class="fa-solid fa-eye-slash text-[#ff6b35]"></i>
          </div>
          <h3 class="font-bold text-white mb-2">No Tracking</h3>
          <p class="text-sm text-slate-400">This site runs entirely clean without any analytic trackers, banners, or cookies.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Detailed Sections -->
      <div class="prose prose-invert max-w-none space-y-12 text-slate-300">
        
        <div class="space-y-6">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white font-heading">1. Information I Collect & How It's Handled</h2>
          <p>
            When you use the calculator engines, everything runs locally on your machine. I don't track or monitor your usage layout.
          </p>
          <p>
            <strong>Website Forms:</strong> If you drop a scaling issue, feature request, or update suggestion using the two forms on this site, that information is sent to a spreadsheet on Google Sheets and backed up on my secure, two-factor authenticated Google Drive. These forms are set up so they do not collect or store any names, email addresses, or personal information. I keep this raw community input around only for the duration of processing and adjusting the conversion numbers, after which it is deleted.
          </p>
          <p>
            <strong>Direct Emails:</strong> If you choose to send me a direct email, your name and the text within your message will land on my email host's secure servers at Proton Mail in Switzerland. Because I run this project entirely alone, I am the only person who will ever see or read your message. I keep your email active strictly while looking into your query or scaling issue. As soon as the matter is completely resolved, your email and its contents are permanently deleted.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="space-y-6">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white font-heading">2. Cookies and Storage</h2>
          <p>
            STLACCESS is completely cookie-free. The only type of browser storage running behind the scenes is:
          </p>
          <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-4">
            <li><strong>LocalStorage:</strong> This lets the site remember your custom entries in the "My Library" feature. This data remains on your hardware, meaning it's completely locked away from me or anyone else.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <div class="space-y-6">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white font-heading">3. Your Data Control</h2>
          <p>
            Because I don't keep your personal information on any server database, you have complete control over your history:
          </p>
          <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-4">
            <li><strong>Portability:</strong> You can see your active numbers directly inside your "My Library" tab.</li>
            <li><strong>Wiping Info:</strong> You can completely clear your saved numbers instantly by clicking "Clear All" in your layout panel or by wiping your local browser site cache.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <div class="space-y-6">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white font-heading">4. Service Providers</h2>
          <p>
            I use a couple of trusted systems to keep the site functional:
          </p>
          <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-4">
            <li><strong>Cloudflare:</strong> For secure deployment, caching speeds, and network security.</li>
            <li><strong>Google Workspace & Proton Mail:</strong> For parsing anonymous form reports and reading direct support requests securely.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <div class="space-y-6">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white font-heading">5. Drop Me a Line</h2>
          <p>
            If you have an issue with privacy setups or want to check how an edge layout works, feel free to open a ticket directly on the GitHub repository. For generic use rules, check out the <a href="/terms" class="text-white border-b border-white/20 hover:text-[#ff6b35] transition-colors">Terms of Service</a>.
          </p>
        </div>

      </div>
    </section>
  </div>
</Layout>